  "body": "I've posted a simple sample, roughly equivalent to the example in this spec, to a branch of node-serialport at:\n\nhttps://github.com/JayBeavers/node-serialport/blob/apiProposal/docs/apiProposal.md\n\nI wanted to highlight the potential differences between what we're working on here and what a very similar API would look like following NodeJS conventions.\n\nThe biggest thing to call out at first is that the SerialPort object would inherit from DuplexStream, so rather than having:\n\nwhatwgport.in.read(...);\nwhatwgport.out.write(...);\n\nwe'd have\n\nnodeport.on('read', ...); // or nodeport.read(...);\nnodeport.write(...);\n\nI'll work towards implementing a simple wrapper over node-serialport that exactly implements this proposed nodejs API to help move this discussion forward.\n\nI also added serialPortDetails.open(options) which is semantically equivalent to calling new SerialPort(serialPortDetails.path, options).\n",
